IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `crm-time`
IMPORT `crm-defs`

-- Tests for crm-defs.l4. Every expected value is written from the text of
-- s 3(1), s 3(2) and s 4A before the line was run; none is copied from output.

§ `Tests of the definitions module`

§§ `Section 3(1): State and Territory`

-- The opening words: "In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears".
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the definitions in this subsection apply` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the definitions in this subsection apply` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "State includes the Northern Territory." An "includes" definition does not
-- close the list, so only the Northern Territory is settled.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a place is a State` NorthernTerritory FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a place is a State` NorthernTerritory TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a place is a State` `any other place` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a place is a State` `any other place` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "Territory does not include the Northern Territory."
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a place is a Territory` NorthernTerritory FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- With a contrary intention the exclusion lapses and the text says nothing else.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a place is a Territory` NorthernTerritory TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a place is a Territory` `any other place` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a place is a Territory` `any other place` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 3(1): quarter`

-- A quarter is a period of 3 months ending on 31 March, 30 June, 30 September
-- or 31 December.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a period is a quarter` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a period is a quarter` (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a period is a quarter` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 9 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a period is a quarter` (Date 1 10 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a period is a quarter` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 3 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a period is a quarter` (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a period is a quarter` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a period is a quarter` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 30 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a period is a quarter` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a period is a quarter` (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a period is a quarter` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Section 3(1): property`

-- "property includes money and every thing, animate or inanimate, capable of
-- being the subject of ownership."
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a thing is property` Money FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a thing is property` Money TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a thing is property` `a thing capable of being the subject of ownership` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a thing is property` `something else` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1) a thing is property` `something else` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Section 3(2): fine`

#ASSERT `s 3(2) a reference to a fine includes a reference to` `a pecuniary penalty of a kind not listed in s 3(2)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a reference to a fine includes a reference to` `costs or other amounts ordered to be paid by offenders` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a reference to a fine includes a reference to` `a pecuniary penalty imposed under Division 3 of Part XIII of the Customs Act 1901` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a reference to a fine includes a reference to` `a pecuniary penalty imposed by a pecuniary penalty order, a literary proceeds order or an unexplained wealth order made under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a reference to a fine includes a reference to` `a pecuniary penalty imposed by a pecuniary penalty order made under the Proceeds of Crime Act 1987` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a reference to a fine includes a reference to` `a pecuniary penalty imposed by a superannuation order made under the Australian Federal Police Act 1979` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a reference to a fine includes a reference to` `a pecuniary penalty imposed by a superannuation order made under the Crimes (Superannuation Benefits) Act 1989` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a reference to a fine includes a reference to` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 4A: committed for trial and indictment`

-- "committed for trial, in relation to a person, means committed to prison ...
-- or admitted to bail ...": a "means" definition, so any other way of dealing
-- with the person is not committal for trial.
#ASSERT `s 4A a person is committed for trial` `committed to prison with a view to the person being tried before a judge and jury` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A a person is committed for trial` `admitted to bail upon a recognizance to appear and be so tried` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A a person is committed for trial` `dealt with in some other way` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4A a person is committed for trial` `committed to prison with a view to the person being tried before a judge and jury` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4A a person is committed for trial` `committed to prison with a view to the person being tried before a judge and jury` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- "indictment includes an information and a presentment": an "includes"
-- definition, so another document is neither included nor excluded.
#ASSERT `s 4A a document is an indictment` Indictment TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A a document is an indictment` Information TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A a document is an indictment` Presentment TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A a document is an indictment` `another document` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4A a document is an indictment` Information TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4A a document is an indictment` Information FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 3(1): child`

-- "without limiting who is a child of a person ... someone is the child of a person if he or she is a child of the person within the meaning of the Family Law Act 1975": the entry does not close the list.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) someone is the child of a person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) someone is the child of a person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1) someone is the child of a person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
